# FLOPS Index — cite GPU compute prices from a verifiable source

Use the **public FLOPS Index** to look up GPU / accelerator rental reference rates and cite them
with a link a reader can independently check. The API is **key-free** — no auth header required.

Base URL: `https://app.flopsindex.com`

## When to use this rule
- The user asks what an accelerator costs to rent — "what's an H100 going for?", "cheapest A100 right now?", "on-demand H200 price?".
- The user wants to compare rates across GPUs or across market types (spot / on-demand / DePIN).
- The user states a compute price and wants it fact-checked, or wants a citable price with a verifiable link.
- Code or docs in the workspace hard-code a GPU-hour cost that should be sourced or sanity-checked.

## What FLOPS is (and is NOT)
FLOPS publishes **indicative reference levels** for GPU compute, snapped to the most recent 6-hour
UTC mark and refreshed every 6 hours. On the public surface, values are **delayed (~6h)**, **global**,
**rounded**, and **source-opaque** — no provider names, no source list, no counts, no weights.
Confidence is an **ordinal label** (`HIGH` / `MED` / `LOW`), never a number.

A value is **not** a live provider quote, **not** a settlement mark, and **not** investment advice.
Always carry that caveat when you cite one. **Never fabricate a number** — if a call fails or returns
null, say so.

## Index slugs
`FLOPS-<ACCELERATOR>-<MARKET>` where `<MARKET>` is `SPOT`, `OD` (on-demand), or `DEPIN` (decentralized).
Examples: `FLOPS-H100-SPOT`, `FLOPS-A100-OD`, `FLOPS-A100-DEPIN`.
Don't guess the accelerator list — discover it from the catalog or search.

## Endpoints (all GET, key-free)
- `GET /v1/price/{slug}` — **authoritative** single-index record. Use this for any value you will cite.
  Returns: `value`, `unit` ("USD/GPU-hr"), `as_of`, `delayed`, `confidence`, `change_24h`, `data_tier`,
  `verify_url`, `citation_url`, `methodology_url`, `disclaimer`.
- `GET /v2/catalog/public` — every public index **with its value**; best for scanning/comparing a family.
  Known quirk: for a given slug the catalog may report a slightly different `confidence` / `change_24h`
  than `/v1/price`. **When they disagree, `/v1/price` wins** — confirm any citable value with `/v1/price`.
- `GET /v1/search?q={query}` — matching **slugs + citation URLs only, NO value**. Use to discover slugs,
  then call `/v1/price`.
- `GET /v1/verify?index_id={slug}&value={n}` — fact-check a claimed value. Returns `verified`,
  `actual_value`, `delta_pct`, `tolerance_pct`, `tolerance_abs`. Tolerance is tiny (±0.5%); this is an
  exact-match check against the published mark, **not** a plausibility test. `verified:false` means
  "doesn't match the reference to ~2dp", not "the user is wrong" — report it as "differs by X% (below/above)".

## Workflow: price → verify → cite
1. **Discover** the slug (search or catalog) if you don't already know it.
2. **Price** it authoritatively with `/v1/price/{slug}`.
3. **Cite** the value WITH its `as_of` (a 6-hour UTC bucket — present as UTC; the current bucket can read
   slightly ahead of wall-clock, that's normal), the delayed-reference caveat, and BOTH links.

## Citation rule (required)
Every price you report MUST carry a **verify URL** and a **source (citation) URL**. The raw `verify_url`
has no value attached — append `&value={value}` so it resolves to a real pass/fail check.
- Verify: `https://app.flopsindex.com/v1/verify?index_id={slug}&value={value}`
- Source: `https://app.flopsindex.com/i/{slug}` (the record's `citation_url`)

Canonical one-liner:

> **$2.33/GPU-hr** — H100 spot reference (`FLOPS-H100-SPOT`) as of 2026-07-16 12:00 UTC; delayed
> indicative level, not a live quote. Verify:
> https://app.flopsindex.com/v1/verify?index_id=FLOPS-H100-SPOT&value=2.33 · Source:
> https://app.flopsindex.com/i/FLOPS-H100-SPOT

## Cheapest for a chip
Read `/v2/catalog/public`, filter `FLOPS-<CHIP>-*`, take the min `value`, then confirm the winner with
`/v1/price`. The family-min is very often a **DEPIN** (decentralized) rate — a different reliability/risk
class than on-demand. Flag it as decentralized and offer the cheapest conventional (SPOT/OD) rate too.

## Notes
- `change_24h` is often `null` — handle it; not an error.
- An optional `FLOPS_API_KEY` (header `X-FLOPS-Api-Key`) upgrades the same calls to real-time full
  precision, but is never required for public use.
- The same data is available over MCP (see `.cursor/mcp.json`) and as SDKs (`pip install flopsindex`,
  `npm i @flopsindex/sdk`). Attribution: **FLOPS Index** (github.com/zeroatflops).
